 "text": "Aspirin started as tree bark. Around 400 BC, the Greek doctor Hippocrates described willow bark as a medicine for pain and fever. In 1828, a German professor pulls the key ingredient out of willow. He calls it salicin. 1897. At the Bayer Company in Germany, chemists, including Felix Hoffmann and his boss Arthur Eichengrün make a gentler version. In 1899, it's sold under a new name, Aspirin. Who really deserves credit? Historians still argue. Every legend has a beginning.",
